{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775330626-pM3G5MzSrDdAePxybUtI","role":"assistant","created":1775330642,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The question asks for the difference between October 3, 1952 and December 18, 1952. Since December 18, 1952 doesn't appear in the data, maybe it's asking about a different format or maybe the December 18, 1952 treasury bills were issued but appear under a different name or maybe I need to look more comprehensively.\n\nLet me search more broadly for any mention of these specific issue dates or look at all the treasury bills to understand what's being asked.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_93f7c9654042751b","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\ndata = json.load(open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1953_03.json'))\n\n# Find all tables with Treasury Bills (look for 'bill' in content)\nfor i, element in enumerate(data['document']['elements']):\n    if element.get('type') == 'table':\n        content = element.get('content')\n        if isinstance(content, str) and 'Amount out-standing' in content and 'Maturity date' in content:\n            print(f'Found at element {i}')\n            # Extract all issue dates\n            import re\n            issue_dates = re.findall(r'<tr><td[^>]*>(\\$?[\\d,]+)</td><td>[^<]+</td><td>([0-9/]+)</td>', content)\n            print('Issue dates:', issue_dates)\n            print()\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
