million outstanding amount. However, the December 18, 1952 bill seems to be missing from the current data. I'll need to investigate why this specific bill doesn't appear in the market quotations table.\n\nI'm exploring alternative representations of the date, checking for variations like \"12/18/52\" or \"December 18\" to ensure I've captured all possible formatting. The current data suggests an absence of this particular bill's information.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_8ee686b3fe8ccf00","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\nimport re\ndata = json.load(open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1953_03.json'))\n\n# Let's examine element 515 more carefully \n# Use a simpler approach - split by rows and parse\n\nelement = data['document']['elements'][515]\ncontent = element.get('content')\n\n# Split into rows and extract data manually\nrows = content.split('<tr>')\nprint(f'Total rows: {len(rows)}')\n\n# Look at each row and extract amounts and issue dates\nfor i, row in enumerate(rows):\n    if '<td>' in row and '</td>' in row:\n        # Get all cell contents\n        cells = row.split('</td>')\n        # Filter to only cells with content\n        cell_contents = []\n        for cell in cells:\n            if '<td' in cell:\n                # Extract content between tags\n                match = re.search(r'<td[^>]*>([^<]+)</td>', cell)\n                if match:\n                    cell_contents.append(match.group(1))\n        \n        if len(cell_contents) >= 3:\n            # Print first 3 cells (amount, maturity, issue date for left bill)\n            print(f'Row {i}: {cell_contents[:3]}')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
